DESCRIPTION >
    Phase 4c (Pattern A row-pull). Per-conversion, picks the last touchpoint's
    attribution fields, replacing the HogQL correlated self-join in
    lastTouchAttribution (api/lib/attribution-engine.js:103-163).
    Built as 3 INDEPENDENT `ASOF LEFT JOIN`s (one per field: utm_source/medium,
    ai_source) rather than a single join picking one touchpoint row, because
    HogQL's actual query computes argMax(column, timestamp) SEPARATELY per
    column — and ClickHouse's argMax SKIPS rows where the column being
    aggregated is NULL when finding the max. That means the live HogQL model
    can synthesize credit from DIFFERENT touchpoints for different fields when
    the chronologically-last touch has a null in one field but an earlier touch
    doesn't (verified empirically on the 4c fixture's visitor Y, see
    tinybird/PHASE4_4C_PLAN.md and the 4c report — NOT a hypothesis, confirmed
    against real fired data both in PostHog and via two failed/passed Tinybird
    query shapes). A single ASOF JOIN picking one whole touchpoint row does NOT
    reproduce this and was empirically WRONG on that case. This is a faithful,
    validated parity port — not a "more correct" rewrite; replicating HogQL's
    actual behavior (including this null-skip quirk) is the explicit Phase 4
    goal per the reconciliation contract.
    A-2 (a single nested LEFT JOIN + argMax, structurally mirroring HogQL's
    literal SQL) was tried first and rejected outright by Tinybird:
    "Unsupported JOIN ON conditions" on the mixed equality+inequality ON clause
    — confirms classic ClickHouse JOIN doesn't accept this shape; ASOF JOIN is
    required either way.
    IDENTITY FIX (rule #19c): the join key was `visitor_id`, but the live
    HogQL self-join (attribution-engine.js:138) joins `pv.distinct_id =
    e_inner.distinct_id`, not visitor_id. Changed all 4 ASOF JOIN keys (and
    the events_by_visitor subquery SELECTs) from visitor_id to distinct_id to
    match the live query exactly. This is a real, previously-latent divergence
    — under single-identity (distinct_id == visitor_id, the only case any
    producer or fixture currently exercises) the two keys are numerically
    identical so no fixture failure surfaced it, but the pipe's structural
    join key was wrong relative to live HogQL.
    SCOPE LIMIT: re-validated (post-fix) only for distinct_id == visitor_id
    (every producer used in the 4c fixture sets only anonymous_id, no separate
    visitor_id/user_id). Server-events.js's user_id-merge path can in
    principle diverge visitor_id from distinct_id (normalize.js:251-253) —
    NOT covered by this pipe's validation, merged-identity case remains
    UNVERIFIED (no fixture exercises it); deferred to the $identify /
    identity-reconciliation backlog item, same as before this fix.
    NOT YET PUSHED (no `tb push`/`tb deploy` run — validated via read-only
    `tb --cloud sql` against the live schema only, per standing no-push rule).

TOKEN "phase4_last_touch_read" READ

NODE last_touch_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        conv.event_id AS conversion_event_id,
        conv.distinct_id,
        conv.timestamp AS conversion_timestamp,
        src.utm_source,
        med.utm_medium,
        camp.utm_campaign,
        ai.ai_source
    FROM
    (
        SELECT event_id, distinct_id, timestamp
        FROM events
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$conversion'
          AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
          AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
    ) AS conv
    ASOF LEFT JOIN
    (
        SELECT distinct_id, timestamp, utm_source FROM events_by_visitor
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview' AND utm_source IS NOT NULL
    ) AS src ON conv.distinct_id = src.distinct_id AND src.timestamp <= conv.timestamp
    ASOF LEFT JOIN
    (
        SELECT distinct_id, timestamp, utm_medium FROM events_by_visitor
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview' AND utm_medium IS NOT NULL
    ) AS med ON conv.distinct_id = med.distinct_id AND med.timestamp <= conv.timestamp
    ASOF LEFT JOIN
    (
        -- nullIf(campaign,'') so the argMax null-skip ENGAGES on Tinybird's empty-string campaign
        -- (Tinybird stores empty utm_campaign as '', not NULL). LIVE reads PostHog where empty
        -- campaign is NULL, so argMax skips the empty touch and credits a later REAL campaign; a bare
        -- `IS NOT NULL` passes '' and diverges. Mirrors #137's non-direct fix. Matches live
        -- argMax(pv.utm_campaign) null-skip (attribution-engine.js:124). source/medium unchanged.
        -- LATENT on the cc-4c fixture (no '' campaigns there, so no in-fixture regression); production
        -- has '' campaigns and would diverge without this.
        SELECT distinct_id, timestamp, nullIf(utm_campaign, '') AS utm_campaign FROM events_by_visitor
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview' AND nullIf(utm_campaign, '') IS NOT NULL
    ) AS camp ON conv.distinct_id = camp.distinct_id AND camp.timestamp <= conv.timestamp
    ASOF LEFT JOIN
    (
        SELECT distinct_id, timestamp, ai_source FROM events_by_visitor
        WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
          AND event_type = '$pageview' AND ai_source IS NOT NULL
    ) AS ai ON conv.distinct_id = ai.distinct_id AND ai.timestamp <= conv.timestamp
    ORDER BY conv.timestamp DESC

TYPE endpoint
